Recommends: nvme-cli
Description: CrystalDiskMark-style storage benchmark driven by fio
 fiomark runs a fixed, well-understood fio suite against a test file and shows
 the six numbers that matter: sequential 1 MiB transfers at queue depth 8,
 random 4 KiB transfers at queue depth 32 with four jobs, and random 4 KiB
 transfers at queue depth 1, each for reads and writes, as MB/s with IOPS and
 mean latency.
 .
 Jobs use direct I/O and io_uring, so the page cache is bypassed. The tool
 resolves the chosen directory to its physical device, checks free space,
 warns about ZFS and tmpfs targets, and removes its test file afterwards. A
 --cli mode prints the same results as a table without needing a display.
